        ("h2", "2. Background"),
        ("h3", "2.1 Test coverage analysis (HW TCA)"),
        ("p", "After assembly, a circuit board goes through several test stages: automated optical inspection (AOI), X-ray inspection (AXI), in-circuit test (ICT) and functional test (FT). Each stage sees different defect types. Test coverage analysis answers the question: <b>if the board has a given manufacturing defect, does any test catch it before it reaches the customer, and how reliably?</b>"),
        ("p", "A passed test only says that the measured properties are fine. If ICT measures a resistor, we know it is present, has the right value and is neither open nor shorted; we know nothing about the components we did not measure [1]. That is why the analysis does not count tests; it takes every possible failure mode and gives it a detection value for each method."),
        ("h3", "2.2 The test methods in the lab"),
        ("table", ["Method", "What it does", "Good at", "Limitations"], [
            ("AOI", "A camera compares the board with a reference image.", "missing part, polarity, alignment, visible solder bridges", "cannot see hidden joints; cannot read the value of unmarked parts"),
            ("AXI", "X-ray image of the solder joints.", "hidden joints, shorts, joint quality", "cannot see the value or function of a part"),
            ("ICT", "A bed-of-nails fixture contacts the test points and measures the parts one by one.", "value, short, open", "needs a test point on every net of the part"),
            ("FT", "The board is powered and its functions are checked through the connectors.", "function at real speed", "often cannot tell which part is faulty")]),
        ("h3", "2.3 S, O, D and action priority (AP)"),
        ("p", "The risk of each failure mode is described by three ratings from 1 to 10, following the AIAG-VDA FMEA handbook [3]:"),
        ("ul", ["<b>S, severity</b>, is rated on the effect: how serious the effect is for the customer. In the lab, S follows from the effect class E1–E9 (appendix A).",
                "<b>O, occurrence</b>, is rated on the cause: how likely the defect is, given the prevention (appendix B).",
                "<b>D, detection</b>: how reliably we catch the defect before the board ships. 1 means almost certainly, 10 means we cannot detect it."]),
        ("p", "All tests run on every board, so <b>the combined detection is the minimum</b> of the methods' D values: D = min(D AOI, D AXI, D ICT, D FT). S, O and D give the action priority AP (H, M or L) from the AIAG-VDA table (appendix C). We do not use RPN = S × O × D: the same RPN can hide very different risks [4]."),
        ("h3", "2.4 Residual risk"),
        ("p", "Risk assessment means identification, analysis and evaluation [5]. Where AP is H or M, we first look for an improvement. What remains after the improvements is the residual risk: it must be documented, with the reason it remains and the decision taken (accepted or action proposed)."),

